# test

Reserved for future PlatformIO tests.

No automated tests are included in `v0.1.0`; validation is currently performed
with firmware builds and physical checks on the Waveshare target hardware.

## Manual valve API checks

Use the current node IP printed after WiFi connects.

1. Reboot the ESP32 and confirm `GET /valves` returns valves 6, 7, and 8 as `"state":"closed"`.
2. Send `PUT /valves/6` with `{"state":"open"}` and confirm relay CH6 activates.
3. Send `PUT /valves/7` with `{"state":"open"}` and confirm relay CH7 activates.
4. Send `PUT /valves/8` with `{"state":"open"}` and confirm relay CH8 activates.
5. Close valves 6, 7, and 8 and confirm relays CH6, CH7, and CH8 deactivate.
6. Send `PUT /valves/8` with `{"state":"bad"}` and confirm HTTP 400.
7. Send `PUT /valves/8` with `{}` and confirm HTTP 400 with `missing_state`.
8. Send `GET /valves/1` and confirm HTTP 404.
9. Confirm `GET /outputs` and `PUT /outputs/relays/1` still work.
10. Confirm `session_active` changes only while valve 8 opens or closes.
11. Confirm valve 6 and valve 7 commands do not start or stop the flowmeter session.
12. Confirm `last_session_l` keeps the closed-session total after valve 8 closes.
13. Confirm `POST /flowmeter/reset-hydrological-year` resets `hydrological_year_l`.
